  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "This is an open-seat race for Washington's 4th Congressional District, a reliably Republican seat covering central Washington including the Yakima Valley, Tri-Cities, and Moses Lake. Incumbent Republican Rep. Dan Newhouse, one of ten House Republicans who voted to impeach President Trump in 2021, announced in December 2025 he would not seek re-election. With no incumbent, a crowded field of 11 candidates is competing in the August 4 top-two primary, with the top two finishers advancing regardless of party. The race is characterized by several Republican candidates vying for the party's base, a unified Democratic candidate, and independents offering alternatives. President Donald Trump has endorsed Amanda McKinney, and the Cook Political Report rates the district as Solid Republican.",
